+# Acceptance Pipeline Runbook
+
+How to run locally
+- Ensure required services are reachable (staging generator, ingest server, Triton host).
+- Configure environment variables:
+  - EVIDENCE_BUCKET (optional)
+  - GEN_STAGING_URL, GEN_PROD_URL, INGEST_SERVER, TRITON_HOST
+- Run: ./ops/scripts/run_acceptance_checks.sh
+
+CI invocation
+- The GitHub workflow .github/workflows/acceptance_pipeline.yml runs the full acceptance pipeline when invoked.
+
+Interpreting results
+- Evidence artifacts are uploaded to s3://$EVIDENCE_BUCKET/acceptance/<run-id>/...
+- Use Grafana dashboard (dashboards/grafana/aegis_autonomy_dashboard.json) to view key metrics.
+- If any step fails, inspect logs in CI job and the evidence manifest (ops/ci/generate_evidence_manifest.py output).
+
+Remediation tips
+- Tokenization mismatch: sync tokenizer binaries between training and serving or regenerate serving tokenizer.
+- Deterministic inference failures: ensure seed propagation in serving, disable non-deterministic optimizations for test runs.
+- High ingest error rates: scale HPA, tune chunk sizes and retry policies, check S3 connectivity.
+- Planner hallucination: review sample intents and adjust planner prompt template, expand allowed tool list, add more strict schema checks.
+
